{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Widow</b> — In the Torah it is written: עֹשֵׂה מִשְׁפָּט יָתוֹם וְאַלְמָנָה (who executes justice for orphan and widow). And he said: 'Judge of the earth' at the beginning of the psalm — this is the exalted interpretation of 'Judge of the earth,' for it is written: כִּי הוּא עֹשֶׂה מִשְׁפָּט גֵּר יָתוֹם וְאַלְמָנָה, and these are the wicked." "<b>The widow and the sojourner they kill, and orphans they murder</b> — Therefore after it: וַיֹּאמְרוּ לֹא יִרְאֶה יָּהּ וְלֹא יָבִין, for they think that the One who forms the eye will not see, and the One who plants the ear will not hear nor understand, in the manner of שִׁמְעוּ שָׁמוֹעַ וְאַל־תָּבִינוּ." "<b>They murder</b> — From the heavy [passive] stem, like: הַמֵּרְצֵחַ הַזֶּה (this murdered one)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 94, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:17.048480955Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}